    "daysLeft": 6,
    "description": "I will be in Guangzhou for the Autumn Canton Fair, and I want a local sourcing partner who truly speaks the language of industrial-grade electronics manufacturing. Your role starts on the show floor: walk the Industrial Electronics halls with me, quickly spot booths whose datasheets, process capabilities and certifications match my specs, and capture clear photos, contacts and technical notes. When a sample is offered, I will depend on you to give an on-the-spot quality check, PCB workmanship, component selection, enclosure tolerances, compliance marks.\n\nI expect an advanced understanding of electronics: you should be comfortable discussing SMT line capabilities, IPC standards, reliability testing, BOM optimisation and MOQ implications with factory engineers, not just sales staff. Native-level Mandarin (Cantonese is a bonus) plus competent English is essential so nothing is lost in translation.\n\nBecause my schedule is tight, I need you in Guangzhou each day of the fair and available for short factory follow-ups in the surrounding area if a lead proves promising. By the end of the event, I will need the following:\n\n• A concise supplier matrix listing at least 10 vetted industrial-electronics manufacturers, with key specs, capabilities and initial price indicators  \n• High-resolution photos of inspected samples annotated with your quality observations  \n• Your prioritised recommendation list with next-step actions\n\nIf you already have established contacts in power electronics, control boards, sensors or ruggedised assemblies, let me know in your reply, those niches align closely with my roadmap.",
